      "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{csc}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\pi =\\frac{2\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\pi }=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
